{{- /*
The key projection for a write that takes its key as an argument.

Every value the law writes goes to the fixture's own key, so the
projection answers that key and ignores what it is handed. Not a
degenerate case of a derived projection but a different fact: a value
whose key is an argument carries no key to project, and the law's claim
— what went in comes back out — is about the value rather than about
where it was put.

The parameter is unnamed for that reason. A body reading it would be
reading a field that is not there.
*/ -}}
{{- define "model.lawfield.KeyOfFixed" -}}
{{ .Name }}: func({{ renderType .Value }}) {{ renderType .Key }} { return fx.{{ .KeyField }}() }
{{- end -}}
